= Fox Engine =
[[File:DDF_semitransparency.png|300px|thumbnail|Deferred shader semitransparency example.<br>Left image is in PES; right is the texture.]]
[[File:DDF_srm.png|300px|thumbnail|Deferred shader specular map example.]]
[[File:DDF_Shaders_Guide.png|300px|thumbnail|Guide to make deferred shaders models look better.]]

Unlike pre-Fox PES which was fully {{tt|forward rendered|Each object is rendered in sequence in one pass.}}, Fox Engine PES uses both forward and {{tt|deferred rendering|A first pass calculates everything in the scene but the lighting, which is 'deferred' to a second pass.}}. Both have downsides:
* '''Deferred rendering doesn't support semitransparency'''; semitransparent textures will instead be '''dithered''' (see image on the right).
* '''Forward-rendered materials will appear blurry when moving'''. There is a workaround for this (see the [[#Material settings|material settings]] section below).

== Material settings ==
Materials for Fox Engine models are configured in the '''Blender materials tab'''.
* Materials can be named anything. You can use the same material for multiple meshes.
* Only the settings under the '''FMDL Material Settings''' header are relevant; none of the regular Blender settings are used.

[[File:Fox_material_settings.png|frameless|400px|none]]
{{div col|colwidth=60em|rules=yes}}
# '''Preset.''' Click to select a material preset. See [[#Other shaders|other shaders]] if you want to use a material without a preset.
# '''Shader and technique.''' These are set automatically when selecting a preset.
# '''Antiblur.''' Eliminates the blur caused by forward materials by creating a slightly smaller duplicate of the mesh with a deferred material on export. If your model has an outline, only the outline needs antiblur.
# '''Alpha and shadow flags.''' These are set by the checkboxes below and you can ignore them if using a preset.
# '''Twosided.''' This will make the game draw both sides of faces instead of only the front.
# '''Transparent.''' Enables (dithered) transparency for deferred materials. Forward materials always allow transparency.
# '''Cast Shadow.''' Makes the mesh cast a shadow.
# '''Invisible.''' Prevents the mesh from being drawn. Invisible meshes can still cast shadows.
# '''Material parameters.''' Material-specific parameters. See material sections below. You may have to add these yourself. Although they have four values, usually only the first one is relevant.
{{div col end}}

== Texture path ==
The '''texture tab''' is where you specify the filenames of your textures and which directories to load them from. Selecting a PES material preset will automatically create corresponding entries for that material in the texture tab.
[[File:Fox_texture_path.png|x250px|frameless|none]]

You can '''omit the file extension''' in the filename. <br>
Select a '''directory preset''' to load a texture from the '''same folder''' as the model; the ''0000'' ID will automatically be substituted on export. (Ignore the ''pes16''.)
* To load a texture from a '''subfolder''' of the team common folder, insert the name of the subfolder between '''''/000/''''' and '''''/sourceimages/''''' in the ''Directory'' field at the bottom.
* The ''PES common folder'' is for loading '''''dummy_nrm.tga''''' and '''''dummy_srm.tga''''' for ''NormalMap_Tex_NRM'' and ''SpecularMap_Tex_LIN'' respectively if you don't want to use those. The plugin sets them to these by default.
* The names of the texture objects in the list '''do not matter''' and do not need to contain the texture type in brackets.

